          %title
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Markovich_Polyakov"} Wikipedia entry
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://phy.princeton.edu/people/alexander-polyakov"} old personal page
                at Princeton (archived
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/APolyakovOldHomepage.jpg"} screenshot
              %blockquote
                %p
                  “My main interests this year &amp;lbrack;1993?&amp;rbrack; were directed towards
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
                  = succeed "\u201C," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tube"} lines of force
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
                  to the Coulomb law at small distances and would give permanent
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
                  of quarks at large distances.”
                %p
                  (cf.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+gauge-string+duality"} Polyakov gauge-string duality
            %li
              %p
                Valery Pokrovsky,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hidden Sasha Polyakov’s life in Statistical and Condensed Matter Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Polyakov’s String: Twenty Five Years After
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0510214"} arXiv:hep-th/0510214
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            Discussing what came to be called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            and the resulting
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+theory"} Liouville theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum geometry of bosonic strings
              %strong 103
              (1981) 207-210 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(81)90743-7"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(81)90743-7
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://qft.itp.ac.ru/polyakov-2.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and for the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum geometry of fermionic strings
              %strong 103
              3 (1981) 211-213 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(81)90744-9"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(81)90744-9
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Introducing
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Belavin"}> Alexander Belavin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"} Alexander Polyakov
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Zamolodchikov"} Alexander Zamolodchikov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Infinite conformal symmetry in two–dimensional quantum field theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(84)90052-X"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(84)90052-X
          %p
            Early discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop"} Wilson loop
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+M.+Polyakov"}> Alexander M. Polyakov
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fermi-Bose transmutation induced by gauge fields
              %strong 03
              03 (1988) 325-328 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217732388000398"}> doi:10.1142/S0217732388000398
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Proposing the identification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+tubes"} flux tubes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"} strings
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            in what came to be known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+correspondence"} AdS-QCD correspondence
            (see
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+gauge-string+duality"} Polyakov gauge-string duality
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String representations and hidden symmetries for gauge fields
                %strong 82
                2 (1979) 247-250 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(79)90747-0"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(79)90747-0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge fields as rings of glue
                %strong 164
                (1980) 171-188 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(80)90507-6"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(80)90507-6
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge Fields and Strings
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9780203755082"} doi:10.1201/9780203755082
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/50871"} oapen:20.500.12657/50871
            %li#Polyakov98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Theory and Quark Confinement
                %strong 68
                (1998) 1-8 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711002"}> arXiv:hep-th/9711002
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0920-5632(98)00135-2"} doi:10.1016/S0920-5632(98)00135-2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The wall of the cave
                %strong 14
                (1999) 645-658 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9809057"}> arXiv:hep-th/9809057
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X99000324"} doi:10.1142/S0217751X99000324
          %p
            eventually leading to the rules of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
          %ul
            %li#GubserKlebanovPolyakov98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Gubser"}> Steven Gubser
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Klebanov"} Igor Klebanov
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"} Alexander Polyakov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gauge theory correlators from non-critical string theory
              %strong 428
              105-114 (1998) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9802109"}> hep-th/9802109
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0370-2693(98)00377-3"} doi:10.1016/S0370-2693(98)00377-3
          %blockquote
            %p Relations between gauge fields and strings present an old, fascinating and unanswered question. The full answer to this question is of great importance for theoretical physics. It will provide us with a theory of quark confinement by explaining the dynamics of color-electric fluxes.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vyacheslav+Rychkov"} Vyacheslav Rychkov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gauge fields-strings duality and the loop equation
              %strong 581
              (2000) 116-134
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0002106"} arXiv:hep-th/0002106
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00183-8"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(00)00183-8
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            and specifically between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/single+trace+operators"} single trace operators
            and
            = succeed "-excitations:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
          %ul
            %li#Polyakov02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gauge Fields and Space-Time
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0110196"} arXiv:hep-th/0110196
          %blockquote
            %p The picture which slowly arises from the above considerations is that of the space-time gradually disappearing in the regions of large curvature. The natural description in this case is provided by a gauge theory in which the basic objects are the texts formed from the gauge-invariant words. The theory provides us with the expectation values assigned to the various texts, words and sentences.
          %blockquote
            %p These expectation values can be calculated either from the gauge theory or from the strongly coupled 2d sigma model. The coupling in this model is proportional to the target space curvature. This target space can be interpreted as a usual continuous space-time only when the curvature is small. As we increase the coupling, this interpretation becomes more and more fuzzy and finally completely meaningless.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Gubser"}> Steven Gubser
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Klebanov"} Igor Klebanov
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"} Alexander Polyakov
              = succeed "," do
                %em A semi-classical limit of the gauge/string correspondence
              %strong 636
              (2002) 99-114 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0204051"}> arXiv:hep-th/0204051
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(02)00373-5"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(02)00373-5
          %p Historical reminiscences:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polyakov"}> Alexander Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Confinement and Liberation
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerardus+%E2%80%99t+Hooft"} Gerardus ’t Hooft
                (ed.)
                %em 50 Years of Yang-Mills Theory
                (2005) 311-329 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0407209"}> arXiv:hep-th/0407209
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789812567147_0013"} doi:10.1142/9789812567147_0013
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/5601"} doi:10.1142/5601
            %li#Polyakov07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+M.+Polyakov"}> Alexander M. Polyakov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Beyond Space-Time
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Quantum Structure of Space and Time
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0602011"} arXiv:hep-th/0602011
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.solvayinstitutes.be/pdf/Proceedings_Physics/23rd_Solvay_Physics.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Polyakov08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+M.+Polyakov"}> Alexander M. Polyakov
                ,
                %em From Quarks to Strings
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0183"}> arXiv:0812.0183
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %p
                published as
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quarks, strings and beyond
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Di+Vecchia"} Paolo Di Vecchia
                et al. (ed.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Birth of String Theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511977725.048"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511977725.048
              %blockquote
                %p
                  “By the end of ’77 it was clear to me that I needed a new strategy &amp;lbrack;for understanding confinement&amp;rbrack; and I became convinced that the way to go was the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/string duality
                %p
                  “I kept thinking about
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/strings dualities
                %p “Since this 5d space must contain the flat 4d subspace in which the gauge theory resides, the natural ansatz for the metric is just the Friedman universe with a certain warp factor. This factor must be determined from the conditions of conformal symmetry on the world sheet. Its dependence on the Liouville mode must be related to the renormalization group flow. As a result we arrive at a fascinating picture – our 4d world is a projection of a more fundamental 5d string theory. &amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack;”
                %p
                  “At this point I was certain that I have found the right language for the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge%2Fstring+duality"} gauge/string duality
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "#Polyakov98"} Polyakov 1998
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702076"} Klebanov 1997
                  in which he related
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D3+branes"} D3 branes
                  described by the supersymmetric Yang Mills theory to the same object described by supergravity. Unfortunately I wrongly thought that the paper is related to matrix theory and I was skeptical about this subject. As a result I have missed this paper which would provide me with a nice special case of my program. This special case was presented little later in full generality by Juan Maldacena (
                  %a{:href => "AdS-CFT+correspondence#Maldacena97a"}> Maldacena 1997
                  ) and his work opened the flood gates.”
